ng dark.\n\n**2. Idle loop (V37E 00E)** — **PROG \"00\" confirmed** on the first attempt; no repeats needed.\n\n**3. Lamp test (V35E)** — at peak: PROG/VERB/NOUN all \"88\", R1/R2/R3 all \"+88888\" (every digit an 8, all signs \"+\"). Ten lamps lit: VEL, NO ATT, ALT, GIMBAL LOCK, TRACKER, PROG, UPLINK ACTY, TEMP, STBY, RESTART. COMP ACTY was *not* among them. Test ended on its own after ~12 s (lamps out, PROG back to 00), though the 88s stayed latched on the digits until the next entry overwrote them.\n\n**4. AGC clock (V16N36E)** — **confirmed counting**:\n- Reading one: R1 `+00002`, R2 `+00013`, R3 `+03037`\n- Reading two (~15 s later): R1 `+00002`, R2 `+00013`, R3 `+04437`\n\nR3 advanced 1400 hundredths = 14.00 s over a ~15 s interval. Clock at 2 h 13 min.\n\n**5. Gimbal angles (V16N20E)** — R1 `+00000`, R2 `+00000`, R3 `+00000`, steady across two reads, no lamps.\n\nTwo things worth noting from the run: the display fills progressively after ENTR, so the first read back is often a partial pattern (I saw `+888` and a leftover `+88888` mid-fill) — every reported value came from a settled follow-up read. And keying over the running V16N36 monitor lit KEY REL intermittently, which cleared itself as each subsequent keystroke was accepted. No OPR ERR occurred at any point, so no RSET was needed.","ttft_ms":3399,"type":"result","duration_ms":221261,"uuid":"53b529a2-eab3-4d66-bf41-d85b407c5488","ttft_stream_ms":2812,"time_to_request_ms":19,"queued_turn_count":0}
